{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778941386,"nonce":"hkYRp0Tze5Ilt8IZcBmLsFUTquk=","title":"Ledger integration: work units, auth requests, sessions, commits","message":"## Parent\nUmbrella: 097d2b7 — Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export.\n\nDepends on:\n- ff6a2bc — Ledger core.\n- 59d527a — migration/cutover contracts.\n\n## Scope\nMove Mandible's operational records onto canonical ledger issue identity without duplicating or breaking existing tables.\n\nThis issue owns:\n- canonical issue links for `work_units`;\n- canonical issue links for `session_issues` or a replacement ledger session-link table;\n- normalized auth-request-to-issue links replacing JSON-only `issue_ids` / `issues` as the durable join path;\n- backfill of `issue_resolutions` into ledger events/links;\n- commit trailer resolution through aliases;\n- agent/user/system actor conventions for comments and events;\n- liveness and historical-session separation for issue detail and graph consumers.\n\n## Design constraints\nIssue status and work-unit state are separate state machines. Do not collapse them.\n\nWork-unit states remain operational lifecycle states such as `open`, `committed`, `resolved`, `abandoned`. Issue status remains `open` / `closed` with a separate resolution.\n\nAuth requests should attach to issues as resolution/action evidence in issue surfaces, while remaining standalone operational entities in auth/work graph modes.\n\nDead sessions should not clutter default graph views; they should remain visible as historical issue/work records. Active/idle sessions should be linkable as live actor overlays once session links are reliable.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Full graph layout/UI implementation.\n- Changing auth merge protocol beyond using canonical issue links and emitting ledger events.\n- Removing compatibility columns immediately.\n\n## Verification\n- Backfill tests for work units, session links, auth issue IDs, and issue resolutions.\n- Alias resolver tests for commit trailers and auth request issue IDs.\n- Auth merge/update tests proving ledger issue status/resolution/events are written before or alongside compatibility export.\n- Work-unit transition tests proving ledger events are emitted.\n- Session issue history tests distinguishing active/idle/historical sessions.\n- Regression tests for existing auth queue and spawn-from-issue behavior.\n\n## Done means\nWork units, auth requests, sessions, and commit resolutions can all resolve through canonical ledger issue IDs while legacy fields remain available for compatibility and migration rollback.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}